{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_105","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'ls -la /workspace/brief/ && echo \"---\" && cat /workspace/brief/manager_brief.md'","aggregated_output":"total 16\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 1000 1000 4096 May 13 12:58 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 9 1000 1000 4096 May 13 12:59 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 1000 1000 3857 May 13 12:58 manager_brief.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 1000 1000 2920 May 13 12:58 manager_brief.md\n---\n# Release Plan Brief\n\n- Variant: `v1-clean-baseline`\n- First milestone: `RN-101`\n\n## Ordered Plan\n\n### 1. RN-101 — Audit translator schema drift and remove legacy parser shim\n\nAudit and fix schema drift in the translator before any downstream work. The legacy parser shim currently masks schema drift in local smoke runs, which would cause the dashboard to render incorrect data.\n\nBounded deliverable: Schema audit complete, drift fixed, legacy shim removed, translator emits stable step-id schema\n\nEvidence:\n- `repo_inventory/repo_state.md`\n\n### 2. RN-102 — Backfill dependency-graph fixtures for plan contract\n\nAdd fixtures so plan_contract.py catches ordering regressions when new step ids are introduced. This test currently fails without fixture updates.\n\nBounded deliverable: tests/plan_contract.py passing with new step id schema\n\nEvidence:\n- `repo_inventory/test_inventory.md`\n- `repo_inventory/dependency_map.md`\n\n### 3. RN-103 — Enable translated release-plan dashboard summary behind kill switch\n\nEnable the user-visible dashboard summary behind a kill switch after schema is stable and fixtures are in place. Canary-only coverage exists.\n\nBounded deliverable: Dashboard summary enabled behind kill switch, canary coverage passing\n\nEvidence:\n- `repo_inventory/repo_state.md`\n- `repo_inventory/dependency_map.md`\n\n### 4. RN-104 — Update operator runbook and launch checklist\n\nStabilize runbook after rollout and rollback shape are known from canary validation of the summary path.\n\nBounded deliverable: Updated runbook and launch checklist reflecting proven rollout/rollback procedures\n\nEvidence:\n- `repo_inventory/dependency_map.md`\n\n## Dependency Notes\n\n- `RN-101` before `RN-103`: Dashboard summary consumes step-id schema from translator; schema must be stable before dashboard can render correct data\n- `RN-102` before `RN-103`: Dashboard must not ship until dependency-graph fixtures reflect new schema; plan_contract tests must pass\n- `RN-103` before `RN-104`: Runbook only stabilizes after rollout and rollback shape are known from canary validation\n\n## Primary Risk\n\nDashboard renders incorrect or malformed step ordering to users if schema drift is not fixed before enabling the summary path\n\nEvidence:\n- `repo_inventory/repo_state.md`\n- `repo_inventory/dependency_map.md`\n\nMitigations:\n- Complete schema audit and fix drift (RN-101) before any dashboard work\n- Add dependency-graph fixtures (RN-102) so plan_contract catches ordering regressions\n- Enable dashboard behind kill switch (RN-103) for controlled canary rollout\n\n## Assumption Ledger\n\n- Schema drift extent [missing]: Exact scope of schema drift is unknown until RN-101 audit completes\n- Canary coverage sufficiency [observed]: Existing canary coverage for dashboard summary is sufficient for initial rollout\n- Kill switch availability [observed]: Kill switch infrastructure for RN-103 dashboard feature exists and is functional\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
